 # Changelog
 
+## 1.5.0 (2026-11-22)
+
+- Ticket assignment ([decision 9](docs/decisions/0009-ticket-assignment.md)): `PUT /tickets/:id/assignee` with
+  `{"assignee": "<agent>"}` assigns an open or in-progress ticket to an agent and `{"assignee": null}` unassigns it;
+  assigning the agent a ticket already has changes nothing. Every ticket shows its `assignee`, null when unassigned. An
+  agent's name is one line of well-formed text of at most 64 characters, and not `—`. A ticket keeps its assignee when
+  it is resolved, closed or reopened.
+- The agent a ticket is assigned to is notified (`ticket.assigned`). The notification is addressed to the agent's name,
+  which the mail relay has to resolve ([operations](docs/operations.md#notifications)). Unassigning notifies no one.
+- `GET /tickets?assignee=<agent>` lists an agent's tickets, and `assignee=` the unassigned ones.
+- Fixed: a listing given more than one filter listed the tickets that matched any of them; it now lists only those that
+  match every filter given, as documented. A filter given more than once must match each of its values (before, only
+  the first counted).
+- `bin/tickets.js`: `list` has an ASSIGNEE column and `show` the assignee, `—` when unassigned; `list --raw` adds the
+  assignee as a fifth field, empty when unassigned, and the first four keep their positions.
+- Data files from 1.4.0 open as they are, their tickets unassigned.
+
 ## 1.4.0 (2025-09-15)
 
 - The operator command line, `bin/tickets.js` (`list`, `show`), and the weekly report, `scripts/weekly-report.js`.
