+An effective change updates the ticket and records who made the change in its audit history (`ticket.assigned` or
+`ticket.unassigned`). Repeating the current assignment leaves the ticket, audit and outbox as they were.
+
+Each effective assignment to an agent enqueues one notification to that agent, which the worker sends: addressed to the
+name exactly as it was assigned ([Operations](operations.md#notifications) says what the mail relay must do with it),
+and quoting the ticket's title as it was at the assignment, even if the title changes before the notification goes.
+Unassigning sends no notification. A notification already enqueued is not withdrawn: when a ticket is unassigned or
+given to someone else before the worker has sent it, each agent it was assigned to in the meantime is still told.
+
+A ticket keeps its assignee through its lifecycle: resolving, closing and reopening it leave the assignee as it was,
+and reopening sends no new assignment notification.
 
