+A change that should tell someone something (a ticket received, a ticket resolved, a ticket assigned to an agent)
+enqueues a notification in the outbox as part of the change ([decision 6](decisions/0006-notification-outbox.md)). The
+worker runs every `WORKER_INTERVAL_MS` and delivers the notifications that are due: with `NOTIFY_FILE` set, it appends
+one JSON line per notification to that file, which the mail relay tails. A line is
+`{ "at", "id", "key", "type", "to", "ticket", "subject", "body" }`, and `type` is `ticket.created`, `ticket.resolved`
+or `ticket.assigned`.
+
+- **Who an assignment notification goes to.** A `ticket.assigned` line's `to` is the agent's name exactly as the ticket
+  was assigned (`"to": "Dana Lee"`), not a mail address: the service keeps no list of agents and never checks that the
+  relay can deliver to a name. The relay has to turn the name into a mailbox, or, where it only delivers to addresses,
+  the help desk assigns tickets by the agent's address (`{"assignee": "dana.lee@example.com"}` is a valid name). A name
+  the relay cannot route is still `sent` in the outbox: the outbox records that the line was written, not that a
+  mailbox received it.
 
